---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PrevNext from '../components/PrevNext.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Brian Thompson, Senior Product Designer"
  description="The convergence of Experience Design, Agent Behavior Design, Systems Architecture, and Rapid Prototyping defines a new kind of practitioner. This is how I think about design."
>

  <Nav />

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section style="padding:120px 48px 80px; max-width:1100px; margin:0 auto;">

    <p style="font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase;
       color:var(--silver); margin:0 0 24px; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;">About</p>

    <h1 class="font-display" style="font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5.5vw,4.8rem);
       color:var(--dark-warm); line-height:1.05; margin:0 0 40px; max-width:680px;">
      I design systems that help people think better.
    </h1>

    <p style="font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--dim-grey); max-width:620px;
       font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; margin:0 0 20px;">
      I'm a Senior Product Designer at Salesforce Financial Services Cloud, where I lead
      AI product design for wealth advisors, bankers, and financial institutions navigating
      some of the most complex, regulated workflows in the world. The work happens at the edge
      of what AI can do today — and what people are ready to trust.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--dim-grey); max-width:620px;
       font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; margin:0;">
      Before Salesforce: I designed for Bank of America, Google, Crunchyroll, Apple, and Audi.
      Each project was a different version of the same question — how do you make a complex
      system feel navigable to the person inside it?
    </p>

  </section>

  <!-- Philosophy -->
  <section style="background:var(--soft-linen); padding:80px 48px;">
    <div style="max-width:1100px; margin:0 auto;">

      <p style="font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase;
         color:var(--silver); margin:0 0 56px; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;">
        Design Philosophy
      </p>

      {[
        ["AI systems should be understandable before they are powerful.",
         "Capability without legibility is a liability. Before shipping power, ship clarity."],
        ["Trust emerges from legibility, not persuasion.",
         "You cannot convince someone to trust a system. You can only make the system worth trusting."],
        ["Designing for AI requires shaping systems and behaviors, not just interfaces.",
         "The interface is the last 10%. The interaction model, the data contract, the error state — those are the design."],
        ["The goal is not automation, but better human judgment.",
         "The measure of a good AI system isn't how much it replaces. It's how much better the person at the center makes decisions."],
      ].map(([principle, commentary]) => (
        <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:48px;
                    padding:36px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(104,103,99,0.15);">
          <p class="font-display" style="font-size:1.25rem; color:var(--dark-warm);
             line-height:1.35; margin:0;">
            {principle}
          </p>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.75; color:var(--dim-grey);
             margin:0; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; padding-top:4px;">
            {commentary}
          </p>
        </div>
      ))}

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Convergence thesis -->
  <section style="padding:80px 48px; max-width:1100px; margin:0 auto;">

    <p style="font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase;
       color:var(--silver); margin:0 0 32px; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;">
      Where the work lives
    </p>

    <p class="font-display" style="font-size:1.7rem; color:var(--dark-warm);
       line-height:1.25; margin:0 0 40px; max-width:620px;">
      The most interesting design problems of the next decade sit at the intersection of
      four disciplines that have never really talked to each other.
    </p>

    <div style="border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; margin:0 0 48px;">
      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); gap:0;">
        {[
          ["Experience Design",     "How people encounter, navigate, and make sense of systems"],
          ["Agent Behavior Design", "How AI systems are prompted, constrained, and evaluated"],
          ["Systems Architecture",  "How data, state, and logic connect across surfaces"],
          ["Rapid Prototyping",     "How ideas become testable things fast enough to matter"],
        ].map(([name, desc]) => (
          <div style="background:var(--soft-linen); padding:36px;">
            <p class="font-display" style="font-size:1.05rem; color:var(--dark-warm);
               margin:0 0 10px; line-height:1.2;">{name}</p>
            <p style="font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.65; color:var(--dark-warm);
               margin:0; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; opacity:0.6;">{desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--dim-grey); max-width:620px;
       font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; margin:0;">
      I think of myself as a practitioner at that intersection — which means being in the
      room when the model behavior is defined, when the data contract is written, when the
      error state is considered. The screen is where the system becomes visible.
      It's rarely where the real design decisions happen.
    </p>

  </section>

  <!-- The thread -->
  <section style="background:var(--soft-linen); padding:80px 48px;">
    <div style="max-width:1100px; margin:0 auto;">

      <p style="font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase;
         color:var(--silver); margin:0 0 32px; font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;">
        The thread
      </p>

      <p style="font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.85; color:var(--dim-grey); max-width:660px;
         font-family:'Inter',sans-serif; margin:0 0 24px;">
        Every project in this portfolio is about the same underlying problem: how do you give
        someone the right information, at the right moment, in a form they can actually act on?
        At Dreamforce, that was 170,000 people and 3,500 sessions. At Audi, a configurator with
        400+ option combinations. At Bank of America, a loan application with 27 entry points.
        At Salesforce today, it's a wealth advisor managing 87 active client relationships while
        an AI system surfaces what matters most.
      </p>

      <p class="font-display" style="font-size:1.3rem; color:var(--dark-warm); margin:0;
         line-height:1.4;">
        The problem scales. The discipline stays the same.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>

  <PrevNext prevTitle="Resume" prevHref="/resume" nextTitle="Home" nextHref="/" />

  <Footer />

</BaseLayout>
